WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.560
DANIELLE BUCKLEY: Hey,
welcome, everybody.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.270
Good morning.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.370
Thanks, all of you,
for making it here.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.480
I'm Danielle Buckley.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.047
I'm the Lead Product
Manager for Google+.

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:15.880
I want to start our
first session today just

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.730
by acknowledging and thanking
those of you in the room who

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:22.270
already use Google+ in
your organizations today.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.030
Show of hands, who already uses?

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.550
Oh, that's great to see.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.050
Awesome.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.000
Thank you, guys.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.810
You've all shown us,
through your experience,

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.530
the power of Google+ to
transform company culture,

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:40.330
to unlock innovation, and to
foster communications across

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.700
organizational boundaries.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.360
You've all also provided us with
valuable feedback on things we

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:52.300
can do to make Google+ work even
better for your organizations.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.530
Thank you.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.230
We appreciate you and
everything you do.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.930
And we're looking forward to
continuing to work with you.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:03.290
Today, we'll talk about how
we're taking your feedback,

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:08.960
and building the next generation
of Google+ for the enterprise.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.970
We'll spend the next
hour together focused

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.970
on three things.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.390
First, I'm going to talk a
little bit about the ways that

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:18.570
companies are using
Google+ today to transform

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.910
their company cultures.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.210
Then-- and for the
first time ever--

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.680
I'm truly excited to be able to
tell you about the 2017 roadmap

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.390
for Google+, what
we've got planned,

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:31.550
and the features that
we're going to be launching

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.880
specifically targeted
at enterprises.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.160
And then finally, we'll close
our session with a panel

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.970
discussion and Q&amp;A where a few
of our customers have kindly

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:44.600
agreed to come and talk about
their experiences using Google+

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:45.890
in their companies.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.050
Over the last few months,
I've had the privilege

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.330
of having a number
of discussions

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.970
with businesses about what's
keeping them up at night.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.670
And across industries,
between departments,

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:05.570
and across geographies,
there is one concern that

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:08.690
comes up time and time again.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.210
How can I make sure that
my company is delivering

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.910
innovation, that we
stay ahead of the curve,

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.920
that we're getting the
most out of our employees?

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.480
In short, how can
I drive innovation?

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.630
At Google, we've seen
that innovation happens

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.680
when you bring people together.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.500
That when you break down
boundaries, and barriers,

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.520
and make it easy for people to
share ideas, exciting things

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.510
happen.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.310
On the Google+ Team, our aim
is to help you drive innovation

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:45.360
by connecting your company,
connecting your people,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:51.400
their ideas, their
interests, their insights.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.080
This means making
it easy for people

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.600
to connect in
different locations

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.450
to share best practices,
for leadership

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.820
to be able to take
the company's pulse,

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.910
and to keep people in the
loop, and for everyone

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:07.780
at every level of your
organization to stay connected,

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:12.270
and to feel like they're
truly part of a team.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.210
With companies more and more
dealing with teams spread out

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:20.010
across the world, employees
who spend most of their time

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:23.610
in the field, large workforces
where it's not always

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:28.560
easy to know what's going
on, or who the experts are,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.690
this can really be a challenge.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:36.300
We believe that Google+ is
uniquely positioned to help.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.780
And we hear this repeated by
those of you who have already

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.120
adopted Google+ in
your organizations.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.180
So we hear things like this.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.540
"We would never have achieved
this level of communication

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.000
and collaboration
without Google+."

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.840
"Google+ breaks down the
invisible walls between

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:02.520
disparate departments, and
creates new connections."

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.400
"Google+ connects us
like never before.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.756
Now we can share expertise,
build relationships."

00:04:11.756 --> 00:04:12.880
This is what gets us going.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.089
This is what brings us
in to work every morning.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.459
That's what gets us excited.

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:22.300
And there are three main ways
that we believe Google+ can

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.630
help connect your company
and drive innovation--

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:29.260
encouraging knowledge
sharing, engaging employees,

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:33.670
and facilitating
secure communication.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.220
First and foremost, our
job is to facilitate

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.320
knowledge sharing.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.860
We do this with tools that allow
teams to better communicate

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:45.380
internally, and smarts
that automatically

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:50.520
uncover untapped knowledge
from across your organization.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.220
This is knowledge
sharing that breaks down

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:58.390
organizational silos, and
connects across geographies.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:01.720
Second, you know that
more engaged employees

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.250
produce better work output.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.710
You tell us this all the time.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:10.310
And Google+ provides a really
easy and scalable channel

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:13.760
for employee engagement
across your organization,

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.200
letting everybody get involved.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.430
Finally, we hear loud
and clear the importance

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.690
of secure communication
within and between teams.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.580
And this is, of course, a
theme that you'll be hearing

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.050
throughout the week this week.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.710
With robust sharing controls,
and dedicated spaces

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:38.360
for private discussions, Google+
provides a reliable, secure,

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:43.080
and scalable channel for your
organization to communicate.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.910
With these three
pillars in mind,

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.510
I'm going to touch briefly on
some of the most widely-used

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.180
features of Google+
in the enterprise,

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.790
and talk a little bit about
how companies are using those

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.890
features today.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:00.910
I'll start off with what's one
of the most widely used tools

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:03.730
in Google+, and something
that's really near and dear

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.520
to my heart, which
is Communities.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.820
Communities and Google+ allow
groups of employees to come

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:14.440
together in a dedicated place to
talk about something specific.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.920
So those of you who are using
Google+ already probably

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.290
already know this, right?

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.710
Communities can be locked
down to just your company.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.904
They can be locked down to
just specific teams or groups

00:06:26.904 --> 00:06:28.570
of people, and made
private, so that you

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.210
can have really secure,
confidential conversations

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.790
in them.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:35.790
We've had lots of
inspiring stories

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:39.570
that come in about companies
using Communities to transform

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:43.340
the way their teams and
their companies work,

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.790
from collaborating on a
team, to allowing employees

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:49.985
to organize social groups,
to sharing customer stories.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:56.420
One of the most interesting
customer examples

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.730
that I've heard
about Communities

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:01.010
comes from a global bank.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:03.140
So this bank was
really struggling with,

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:06.972
how do we find out about
maintenance issues at our ATMs?

00:07:06.972 --> 00:07:08.930
How do we make sure that
we're deploying people

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:10.760
to go fix them?

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:14.120
And the thing that they latched
on to as a potential solution

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.660
for this was, we've actually got
a whole ton of branch employees

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.880
who are already distributed
all across the globe.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.410
What if we could
leverage those employees?

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.490
So what they did was they
enrolled all of their branch

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:28.910
employees into a large
community-- so 30,000 employees

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:30.230
in a community.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:32.780
And all of them were then
transformed into, essentially,

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:33.995
ATM mystery shoppers.

00:07:33.995 --> 00:07:37.940
So they were able to take
pictures, and make posts,

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:41.300
and file complaints when they
noticed issues in the field.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.950
That then allowed
maintenance personnel

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.410
to go out and
address those issues.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.190
Problem solved.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:57.160
Of course, we also rely on
Communities at Google, as well.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.010
So teams will often
have Communities

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.200
for their own internal
discussion talked about,

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.600
hey, what features
should we be developing?

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.030
What are you hearing
from customers?

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:09.030
How are we addressing
this particular concerns--

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:12.510
really get discussion
going on specific teams.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:15.090
Then there's folks who
serve Google broadly, right?

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.340
The Google Travel
Team is a team that

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.560
helps Googlers who are
traveling around the globe

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.280
to visit other
offices or customers.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.730
They've got a community
where anyone, any Googler,

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.800
can ask a question, hey,
what do I do about customs?

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.040
Or does anybody know how to
get a visa to this place?

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.770
I've got a surprise
trip coming up.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:36.240
And then other Googlers are
able to answer their questions

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.299
really quickly.

00:08:37.299 --> 00:08:39.090
It allows for a much
more scalable solution

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:42.260
to serving their needs.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:44.250
One thing close to my
heart, product managers

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.290
also have a
community, where we're

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:50.450
able to share tips, and tricks,
and how to do our job better.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.750
Like, what's something
that works for you?

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.299
I'm having this issue.

00:08:54.299 --> 00:08:55.590
How would you guys approach it?

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.423
And we're able to really
easily communicate,

00:08:57.423 --> 00:08:59.010
even though product
managers tend

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:02.620
to be distributed one in one
team, one in another team.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.320
And so it can,
potentially, be very

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.480
difficult to share
knowledge and best practices

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.160
across that kind of
a distributed group.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.200
So that's Communities.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:17.590
Another tool we offer to
facilitate knowledge sharing

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:20.380
is what's called Collections.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.660
Those of you who have used
Google+ in the past couple

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.660
of years probably noticed
the addition of this.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.790
Collections are
individual streams.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:31.390
So a particular employee
can create a collection

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:35.230
about a specific topic,
sort of like micro blogs.

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:37.210
And they allow folks
to focus their message

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:39.290
on a specific topic.

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:41.530
So for example, one
customer executive

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:44.170
uses a collection
to share things

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:46.150
that he's hearing
about industry trends,

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:49.330
and get them out to the whole
company in a lightweight way

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:52.900
that doesn't require
him to email everybody,

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:56.920
but in a way that
facilitates sharing.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:10:00.130
At Google, we've got
a developer advocate

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:08.160
who started a collection called
HGRW, How Google Really Works.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.420
How does Google really work?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:13.090
Well, he finds posts that
other people are making--

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.540
here's how we do this
in this part of Google.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:18.330
Here's how we develop
product over here.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.312
Here's how we're
developing these concerns.

00:10:21.312 --> 00:10:23.520
And really, by sharing this
into a single collection,

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.520
he's brought together a
whole bunch of knowledge

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.055
from across Google about what
makes our culture unique.

00:10:35.645 --> 00:10:38.350
At a higher level, when
you look at all of this,

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:42.250
and bring it all together,
Google+ provides a window

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:47.730
for executives to understand
employee sentiment.

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:50.730
So one of the things
that can be hard

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:54.600
when you're in headquarters
is figuring out,

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:56.680
what's really going
on with my employees?

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.220
How are they really feeling?

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.220
So for example, you could
monitor employee chatter

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:05.630
in Communities, figure out
what are their real concerns,

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:08.040
potentially highlight
specific needs for improvement

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.100
in your organization.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:13.280
Leaders can take advantage
of features like polls

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.614
to test ideas.

00:11:14.614 --> 00:11:17.030
You know, we're thinking about
marketing this new product.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.900
We've got a few names.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.350
What do you guys
think about this?

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:26.500
And to get a sense of employees
reactions to suggestions.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.750
For example, there
was an airline

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:32.170
who was finding it really
pretty difficult to connect

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:36.100
with their employees
who are on flight crews,

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:38.260
or out in the field
in operations.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:42.400
These folks are on the
go all across the globe,

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:45.330
really difficult to talk
to all of them at once.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:48.430
And so they set up global
and regional communities

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.960
where the CEO and other leaders
were able to post messages

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:55.630
that they were able to get to
everybody all across the globe,

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:57.880
and interact with their
employees on the go

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:59.841
since they had the mobile apps.

00:11:59.841 --> 00:12:01.590
And then the corporate
communications team

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.460
is able to see things
that people shared

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:05.497
into that community and
gauge their response,

00:12:05.497 --> 00:12:08.080
and kind of keep their finger
on the pulse of what's happening

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.498
in their organization.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.060
Finally, the home
stream and notifications

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:19.230
ensure that employees don't
miss out on important messages,

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:22.410
regardless of where in
the company they are.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:26.970
So these actions, as you know
if you already use Google+,

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:30.480
include updates from things
that they're already following,

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:33.270
as well as smart suggestions for
things across the company that

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:36.360
they should be aware of, but
aren't necessarily following

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.710
yet.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:41.310
For example, many executives
at Google post publicly--

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:44.340
restricted to
google.com, of course--

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:46.377
when they want to
communicate with their teams.

00:12:46.377 --> 00:12:48.210
And this gives them a
channel to communicate

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:50.418
on a range of subjects that
they wouldn't necessarily

00:12:50.418 --> 00:12:55.370
want to send a full,
heavyweight email on.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.450
The ability for these posts
to show up in the home stream,

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:00.590
and to notifications,
means that they're

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.650
able to communicate really
directly with a lot of people.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.470
I want to change
gears, momentarily,

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:14.100
to talk about 2016 for Google+
because we had a really

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:14.900
exciting year.

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:22.230
Last year, among a
number of enhancements,

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.210
we launched three major things.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.225
And I'm missing something
on here-- ah, great.

00:13:26.225 --> 00:13:29.430
The most important
one was missing.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:33.120
Big milestone for us-- we
launched Google+ as a G Suite

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.820
core service last August.

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:38.790
And we were privileged
and excited to join

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:43.860
the ranks of products
like Calendar and Gmail

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:47.010
that are well-used and loved by
our enterprises-- very exciting

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:48.700
for us.

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:52.200
We also rolled out the
new Google+ web UI to all

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:55.290
of our users, including
enterprise customers,

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.510
as well as consumers.

00:13:57.510 --> 00:14:02.940
This new web UI moves really
seamlessly from desktop

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.140
to mobile--

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.630
really great for
employees on the go.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:09.690
It also puts
knowledge-sharing, specifically

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:14.280
through Communities and through
Collections, front and center

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:18.000
to help companies make sure
that the folks that need to be

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.970
in the know stay in the know.

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:22.980
Finally, we made
significant improvements

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.170
to community moderation.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:29.010
So this was a set of tools that
enabled community moderators

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:32.865
to take the reins of content
coming into their Communities.

00:14:32.865 --> 00:14:35.130
This including things
like the ability

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:38.400
to approve every post that
comes into your community

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.175
before it shows up--

00:14:40.175 --> 00:14:41.550
really good for
Communities where

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:43.930
you want to lock
down the message,

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:46.080
or to individually
white-list users.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:49.070
You may have a set of users who
you know are great, and should

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.820
be posting into the
community, and another

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:53.910
set who you know you want to
review them a little more.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.490
So we're excited to have this
enhanced suite of community

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:57.510
moderation tools.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.930
All that said, we firmly believe
that this is just the beginning

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:05.950
for Google+.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:09.840
You guys have all given
us lots of feedback.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.990
And we've used that feedback
to develop a roadmap

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:16.620
for the next year that focuses
on the needs of enterprises

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:19.050
like yours.

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:23.580
So for the first time ever, I'm
really excited to today be able

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:27.336
to talk about the
upcoming roadmap for 2017,

00:15:27.336 --> 00:15:28.710
what we're going
to be launching,

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:33.134
specifically for
enterprises using Google+.

00:15:33.134 --> 00:15:35.560
And then, at this
point, our lawyers

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:38.260
asked me to remind you
that, while we strive

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:40.390
to meet the timelines that
I'm going to talk about,

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:43.090
and to launch all
these features,

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:45.820
all this is subject to
change without notice--

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.170
fine print.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.910
[LAUGHING]

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:50.940
Really, the lawyer
line gets a laugh.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.490
This is when you know
you need better jokes.

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:55.865
[LAUGHING]

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:00.440
So first, I want to
talk about enhancements

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:03.640
to knowledge sharing.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:06.170
So Google+ today already
provides the ability

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:09.620
for your employees to tap into
knowledge and expertise from

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:12.800
across your organization that
they wouldn't otherwise have

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:14.850
access to.

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:16.590
Over the next year,
we'll continue

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:19.710
to use Google smarts
to enhance our ability

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:22.950
to deliver world-class
connectedness and knowledge

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:27.570
sharing across your enterprise,
for example, by tailoring

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:31.380
recommended Collections and
Communities to the things that

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:35.240
are most important
in your company.

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:37.490
This investment in
implying Google smarts

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:41.540
to your organization will make
it even easier for employees

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:45.620
anywhere in your company to
find the content, communities,

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.830
and people that they should
be in touch with to be

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:51.700
at their most innovative.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:55.590
And then let's talk about
employee engagement.

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:58.770
This can be sort of
a nebulous subject.

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:02.360
You all want
employee engagement.

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:05.900
But how do you actually know
if your employees are engaged,

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.934
or if they're
engaged on Google+?

00:17:07.934 --> 00:17:10.715
It can be tough.

00:17:10.715 --> 00:17:12.839
So we're excited to announce
that we're going to be

00:17:12.839 --> 00:17:15.450
introducing, in
the admin console,

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:18.839
tools that directly allow
you to measure the engagement

00:17:18.839 --> 00:17:22.107
of your employees on Google+.

00:17:22.107 --> 00:17:27.119
These metrics will allow admins
to dig into overall activity

00:17:27.119 --> 00:17:28.910
in your domain.

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:32.090
For example, how
many posts are there?

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:33.620
How many comments are there?

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.130
How many plus ones?

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:40.840
How many folks are active
on G+ on any given day?

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:44.772
Which Communities
have the most members?

00:17:44.772 --> 00:17:46.230
We're also going
to give you access

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:47.550
to user-level statistics.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:51.000
So who in my company
is really active here?

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.140
Who are the drivers?

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:55.280
Who are the opinion leaders?

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.935
And finally, down
the road, we'll

00:17:56.935 --> 00:17:59.930
also introduce
community-level metrics,

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:05.000
so you can see engagement
in particular Communities.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:10.140
Finally, let's talk a bit
about secure communication.

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:12.870
One thing we've heard
from many of you--

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:17.160
and especially those in
highly-regulated industries--

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:20.910
is the importance of being
able to track user activity

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.840
at a transaction level.

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:26.370
That's like the really
detailed stuff, right?

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:30.660
This year, will introduce an
enterprise log API that will

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:34.020
allow your company, or
an authorized partner,

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:39.500
to track Google+ activity of
specified users in your domain.

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.560
For example, you'll be
able to track in detail,

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:44.870
which post did a user make?

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:46.310
When did they edit them?

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.290
Which comments did they make?

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.990
When did they remove
or delete those?

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:53.554
Giving you full trail
of their activity.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:19:00.180
This one I'm really
excited about.

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:03.570
In addition to being able
to track employee activity,

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:06.570
we know many of you would like
to have further control over

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:10.440
the extent to which your
employees are able to interact

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:14.395
with the outside
world on Google+.

00:19:14.395 --> 00:19:16.130
We're excited to
announce that we're

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:20.240
in the process of developing new
admin settings that will allow

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:22.790
you to select the level
of openness that's

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:25.730
right for your company.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:29.090
So for this, there are going
to be three levels of options.

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:32.860
The first level-- and this is
the current setting for all

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:37.232
domains using Google+--
is what we call public.

00:19:37.232 --> 00:19:38.990
Public means that
all of your users

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:41.990
are able to freely interact
within your domain,

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.450
as well as outside
of your domain.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.320
They, of course,
still have the ability

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:49.740
to control who they share
with, such that only people

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.810
within the domain can see it.

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:53.490
They can still lock
down Communities

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.860
to within just your domain.

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:57.540
But in addition,
they have the ability

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:01.650
to explore content shared
outside of their domain,

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:04.410
as well as to talk
to customers who

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:08.190
may be in the outside world, to
post on topics in which they're

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.580
thought leaders.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:14.230
The second option-- and this is
where we get into what's new--

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:16.550
is a discovery mode.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:20.260
So in this mode, users
can still see content

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:22.270
that's being posted externally.

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:23.770
So they're able
to see how people

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:25.520
are talking about your company.

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:28.690
They're able to see what people
are posting in your industry.

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:30.940
But they're restricted
from sharing or commenting

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:31.997
externally.

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:38.300
This option is potentially
useful for folks

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:41.570
who maybe shouldn't
have a public presence,

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:44.480
but still want to be able to
stay on top of what's happening

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:48.100
outside of your organization.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:51.280
The final option is what
we call walled garden.

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:54.310
This is the most locked
down of the options.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:59.080
And in this mode, users aren't
able to see external content

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:02.860
in recommendations, in
suggestions, in Google+ search.

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.650
And they, of course, aren't
able to post, or comment,

00:21:05.650 --> 00:21:09.110
or plus one externally either.

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:13.250
Each of these options can be
customizable at an OU level.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.200
So if you wanted your
marketing department

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:18.200
to be able to post
externally, but thought

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:21.803
that R&amp;D would be better served
by a discovery mode setting,

00:21:21.803 --> 00:21:24.011
that's going to be an option
that's available to you.

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:31.490
Finally, we've heard lots
of input from those of you

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:34.700
who would like the ability to
tighten down security, and be

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:37.430
sure of who's involved
in the conversation,

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:40.850
but who still want to be able to
collaborate with people outside

00:21:40.850 --> 00:21:42.680
of your domain.

00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:46.220
For example, you may want to
brainstorm potential ideas

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.000
with clients.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.540
You may want to work
with partner teams.

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:54.850
You may want to talk to
employees in a sister company.

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:58.300
To allow you to do that
safely and securely, we're

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:01.570
introducing multi-domain
Communities.

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:04.750
So these are Communities
that are domain restricted.

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:08.500
But they're restricted
to multiple domains.

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:11.980
So you can have that
secure conversation,

00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:14.650
be sure that things
aren't being leaked,

00:22:14.650 --> 00:22:18.127
that people outside of the
domain aren't being invited.

00:22:18.127 --> 00:22:20.710
But you're able to do that with
the companies that we know you

00:22:20.710 --> 00:22:24.060
work with in your
day-to-day jobs--

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.450
so securely restricted,
but now collaborative too.

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:31.972
All right, I know what
you've been waiting for.

00:22:31.972 --> 00:22:33.430
I said we're going
to tell you when

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:34.596
we were shipping this thing.

00:22:34.596 --> 00:22:36.280
So I guess I should
actually do that.

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:42.600
So we'll start by introducing
domain-level user metrics

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:44.670
in Q2.

00:22:44.670 --> 00:22:47.160
In Q3, things start
to really get real.

00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:50.280
So you'll see
multi-domain Communities,

00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:55.710
user-level usage metrics, and
the Google+ enterprise log API.

00:22:55.710 --> 00:22:58.050
And then in Q4,
walled garden, which

00:22:58.050 --> 00:23:01.249
gives you three settings
on domain openness,

00:23:01.249 --> 00:23:02.040
is going to launch.

00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:04.210
So it's an exciting year for us.

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:06.240
And we hope, an exciting
year for you, as well.

00:23:09.170 --> 00:23:12.230
By helping you break down
barriers and share knowledge

00:23:12.230 --> 00:23:15.110
across your company,
engage all your employees,

00:23:15.110 --> 00:23:17.750
no matter their
level or location,

00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:20.360
and providing secure
communications needed

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:24.930
to discuss new ideas, we believe
Google+ can help your company

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:29.310
come together and do
more innovative work.

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:31.860
And while I'm incredibly
excited about all

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:35.620
we've been able to
accomplish together already,

00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:39.240
I'm even more excited
about what's to come.

00:23:39.240 --> 00:23:43.090
Your partnership through
your trial, your feedback,

00:23:43.090 --> 00:23:47.700
your drive to push to get even
better is helping us improve

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:50.095
Google+ and make it even
better serve your enterprises.

00:23:50.095 --> 00:23:51.660
So thank you for that.

00:23:54.789 --> 00:23:58.030
We're looking forward to
unlocking even more innovation

00:23:58.030 --> 00:23:59.809
in your enterprises together.

00:23:59.809 --> 00:24:01.600
And thanks, everybody,
for taking the time,

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:04.270
and choosing to come
here about Google+.

